WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0007: fixes from the first desktop playtest (on top of 0001-0006).

- wowbg3_tav.rs: Tav's pose blended between BG3's last two records at WoW's frame rate, one BG3
  frame back on BG3's capture clock (palettes and object transforms, at most a quarter frame of
  extrapolation); her cut-outs (hair, fur, lace) cut at BG3's 0.5 instead of WoW's 224/255, with
  coverage-preserving mips; her root published as TavFeet after her pose (set TavPose).
  Knobs: WOW_BG3_TAV_SMOOTH=off, WOW_BG3_TAV_TRACE=<frames>, WOW_BG3_TAV_CUTOFF=<0..1>.
- blob_shadow.rs: in world mode the own (hidden) body's blob shadow lies under Tav, at her root
  of the same frame, ordered after her pose.
- wowbg3_lead.rs: bg3input.bin BGI2 (right clicks) besides BGI1; a BG3 right click over a WoW
  unit, corpse or object is WoW's right click (interact), over WoW's UI a right click there; out
  of reach the hidden body walks there (Click to Move's walk, on in world mode) and holds while
  the walk or the NPC window lasts (20 yd leash). WOW_BG3_INPUT=<file> for tests.
- player/approach.rs: Approach::toward_object(), for that hold.
- target/hover.rs, target/hover_probe.rs, ui_script/input.rs: BG3's cursor (the external
  pointer, world mode only) wins over benilla's own window cursor for the picks and the UI feed.

